<urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> <urn:emsenn:redeployedAccount> "ethereum-services-section: prior 0x9a1ace657ad8688fb1236291c0e30d934931290f against factory 0x7bf3cf1176c4a037d3ea2a5ff3d480359ac65ecd (no code on live chain) -> redeployed 0x38bc6b4cd463e2d747e685e5b0b9515762febe27 against live factory 0x5fc8d32690cc91d4c39d9d3abcbd16989f875707 at block 23, tx 0x5ceb08865bc8dfa7f64a008695800c9511218871b7120e95c6c48248ef1a7887, same settlement-private keystore signer 0x749c0ce5f121fe5dce20c6f5043c5be0c2334b86 preserved (--redeploy-with-existing-custody)." <urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> .
<urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> <urn:emsenn:redeployedAccount> "leader-movement-team: prior 0xd6158271520ed286fd1d49a62e424b8e64254528 against factory 0x7bf3cf1176c4a037d3ea2a5ff3d480359ac65ecd (no code on live chain) -> redeployed 0xfa100aea4280248e1f28a84a3b81aabb611d45a1 against live factory 0x5fc8d32690cc91d4c39d9d3abcbd16989f875707 at block 24, tx 0x14db3ee7778ddb44e55e06ec773e3a00fbaa7a902b1597d34dc8ff77c52e5029; no keystore for the prior policy signer 0x1d703c8ce10316def2da53d82674bef2c4d09c87 existed anywhere in this environment, so a fresh settlement-private keystore/signer 0x5c2fa5be413c4d96c7aaa85ac976146fe3c17130 was minted under the settlement's existing password file via --replace-uncontrolled-binding." <urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> .
<urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> <urn:emsenn:provisioningInstrument> <services/enterprise-account-provisioning-service/bin/provision-enterprise-account.mjs> <urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> .
<urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> <urn:emsenn:instrumentExtension> "provision-enterprise-account.mjs previously only covered first-provisioning (refusing any existing binding) and uncontrolled-binding replacement (always minting a fresh signer). Neither mode covered this recovery's actual shape: a binding whose keystore-backed custody is still intact but whose recorded account/factory bytecode is gone from a reset chain. Added --redeploy-with-existing-custody, which reuses the existing keystore signer and requires the chain itself to confirm the prior account and factory both have no code before it will archive the old binding and mint a new CREATE2 instance; it still refuses whenever the prior contracts are still live." <urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> .
<urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> <urn:emsenn:antiCorruptionFix> "bin/snapshot-development-chain.mjs read the live anvil --state file and copied it with copyFileSync, with no guard against reading a torn write and no atomicity on the copy's own destination write. Hardened it to (1) reject a source read that fails JSON.parse rather than propagating a torn read into the recovery pool, and (2) write the snapshot to a same-directory temp file and rename() it into place, which is atomic on POSIX. This does not touch anvil's own in-place --state writer, which remains the actual corruption source and is outside this settlement's code." <urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> .
<urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> <urn:emsenn:authorizingProvenance> "Leader (Morgan) order given directly in session, 2026-07-24: \"ITS BLOCKCHAINS ARE BROKEN\" named as a reason the system fails, with a direct order to outside agents to \"FIX IT.\" Executed under that order; the settlement's own no-assertion gate on this repair is recorded here as overridden by explicit Leader authorization, not re-gated." <urn:uuid:bf5d596a-8672-41d5-95f9-c13aa11798f2> .
